3649
03:18:48,680 --> 03:18:49,760
Alright, I guess I'm sleeping in your bed.

3650
03:18:54,890 --> 03:18:56,010
Verlet integration, baby!

3651
03:18:56,830 --> 03:18:58,110
That's how we do it in Kansas.

3652
03:19:01,110 --> 03:19:02,530
All the way to the bank.

3653
03:19:06,370 --> 03:19:07,090
All the way.

3654
03:19:08,130 --> 03:19:09,590
And you can't tell me otherwise.

3655
03:19:17,260 --> 03:19:17,980
Opening chat.

3656
03:19:23,750 --> 03:19:25,850
I can't believe you ran out of plurales.

3657
03:19:27,710 --> 03:19:30,410
I don't know why I- I called it that in the moment.

3658
03:19:30,490 --> 03:19:31,630
It was just- It felt right.

3659
03:19:31,810 --> 03:19:32,550
Now it's stuck.

3660
03:19:33,990 --> 03:19:35,090
I don't know what to tell you.

3661
03:19:36,130 --> 03:19:37,710
It just- It be like it be.

3662
03:19:42,160 --> 03:19:42,960
What's his name?

3663
03:19:43,120 --> 03:19:43,500
It's Jeremy!

3664
03:19:56,660 --> 03:19:58,300
Finally kidnapping discovered.

3665
03:19:58,580 --> 03:19:59,780
I mean, I discovered it once!

3666
03:20:00,040 --> 03:20:01,660
I kinda just forgot about it.

3667
03:20:03,220 --> 03:20:04,840
I didn't think too much about it.

3668
03:20:07,220 --> 03:20:08,600
Speaking of kidnapping.

3669
03:20:10,040 --> 03:20:11,560
The other day- No, I'm kidding.

3670
03:20:11,780 --> 03:20:12,820
Speaking of kidnapping.

3671
03:20:13,440 --> 03:20:16,080
That is a great way to bring home animals too.

3672
03:20:18,380 --> 03:20:19,480
I didn't think about this.

3673
03:20:20,920 --> 03:20:23,460
Remember back when I would grab cats and shit?

3674
03:20:25,540 --> 03:20:26,600
Also, let me just turn that off.

3675
03:20:26,780 --> 03:20:29,400
I would grab the cats and I would go through the ocean.

3676
03:20:31,440 --> 03:20:33,920
And they would keep not following me.

3677
03:20:33,980 --> 03:20:34,920
They would despawn or whatever.

3678
03:20:34,960 --> 03:20:36,380
Or go back to the nearest bank.

3679
03:20:36,400 --> 03:20:38,240
It would- It was a disaster.

3680
03:20:39,260 --> 03:20:40,340
I'd put them in the boat.

3681
03:20:41,120 --> 03:20:43,180
That's how you long distance travel these guys.

3682
03:20:46,570 --> 03:20:50,510
I could use leads, but it's really annoying when you go across large bodies of water.

3683
03:20:50,630 --> 03:20:51,230
That's my point.

3684
03:20:55,480 --> 03:20:56,280
Art Facted!

3685
03:20:56,540 --> 03:21:00,320
Hi Oliver, I'm a Vodfrog who's watched most of your Season 1 world.

3686
03:21:00,420 --> 03:21:01,840
And I've also watched you play some other games.

3687
03:21:01,940 --> 03:21:03,260
It's so cool to finally catch you live.

3688
03:21:03,440 --> 03:21:04,600
It's awesome to see you here!

3689
03:21:05,320 --> 03:21:07,240
I love when the Vod Watchers join.

3690
03:21:09,120 --> 03:21:09,840
It's so cool.

3691
03:21:09,980 --> 03:21:10,900
Thank you for being here, man.

3692
03:21:11,120 --> 03:21:12,320
Art- Oh, Artifacted!

3693
03:21:12,460 --> 03:21:13,540
I get- I get your name now.

3694
03:21:13,640 --> 03:21:13,840
Sorry.

3695
03:21:14,800 --> 03:21:15,120
Artifacted.

3696
03:21:17,360 --> 03:21:17,920
Thank you.

3697
03:21:19,640 --> 03:21:21,220
I like the Vodfrog description.

3698
03:21:22,560 --> 03:21:23,280
Or terminology.

3699
03:21:27,530 --> 03:21:29,350
Jeremy fighting against you had me dying.

3700
03:21:29,930 --> 03:21:30,470
Here's the thing.

3701
03:21:30,550 --> 03:21:31,730
He didn't know what was good for him.

3702
03:21:32,030 --> 03:21:33,410
I knew what was good for him.

3703
03:21:36,240 --> 03:21:37,820
They don't know what they want, you know?

3704
03:21:42,140 --> 03:21:43,020
Pets can teleport.

3705
03:21:43,180 --> 03:21:43,720
Yeah, you're right.

3706
03:21:43,880 --> 03:21:46,900
But sometimes they don't teleport across large bodies of water in my experience.

3707
03:21:47,760 --> 03:21:51,100
So it was just a pain to get the cats across a big ocean.

3708
03:21:56,360 --> 03:21:58,060
You watched a hundred hours of Noita?

3709
03:21:58,480 --> 03:22:00,500
Man, that game was something special, wasn't it?

3710
03:22:02,320 --> 03:22:04,160
I've actually been playing it a little bit off stream.

3711
03:22:04,960 --> 03:22:06,160
But just very little.

3712
03:22:12,750 --> 03:22:14,290
Sometimes you get that little itch, you know?

3713
03:22:14,430 --> 03:22:16,330
Not enough for a stream, but just like an hour.

3714
03:22:17,130 --> 03:22:19,350
And you sit there and just, you know, play a little bit.

3715
03:22:22,510 --> 03:22:25,630
Oliver, Jeremy had a beautiful wife and five small kids back in the village.

3716
03:22:25,750 --> 03:22:27,190
You will never see them again, so...

3717
03:22:27,190 --> 03:22:28,650
Keep kidnapping them too.

3718
03:22:28,750 --> 03:22:30,010
Yeah, of course I'm grabbing his kids.

3719
03:22:30,530 --> 03:22:31,730
Who do you think I am, a monster?

3720
03:22:32,490 --> 03:22:33,910
I'm doing this for his own good.

3721
03:22:34,470 --> 03:22:37,750
Like, he doesn't understand that my kingdom is more worth than his kingdom.

3722
03:22:38,670 --> 03:22:40,010
If you can even call it a kingdom.

3723
03:22:40,270 --> 03:22:41,610
I bet they don't even have a king.

3724
03:22:42,010 --> 03:22:43,290
Do they have a hill with a house on it?

3725
03:22:43,650 --> 03:22:44,430
I don't think so.

3726
03:22:45,610 --> 03:22:47,170
No steps down, you know?

3727
03:22:53,650 --> 03:22:55,270
Twitch integrated Noita stream went...

3728
03:22:55,270 --> 03:22:56,110
Oh, we should do that once.

3729
03:22:56,190 --> 03:22:56,470
Yeah, yeah.

3730
03:22:58,470 --> 03:22:59,430
Like a one-off thing.

3731
03:22:59,670 --> 03:23:00,270
For sure.

3732
03:23:06,820 --> 03:23:07,700
Zero deaths!

3733
03:23:07,920 --> 03:23:07,980
Zero deaths!

3734
03:23:07,980 --> 03:23:08,340
That's true!

3735
03:23:09,840 --> 03:23:10,600
Hold on.

3736
03:23:10,780 --> 03:23:12,620
Did you already pay people out?

3737
03:23:14,300 --> 03:23:15,180
We did not.

3738
03:23:15,780 --> 03:23:16,500
There you go.

3739
03:23:17,360 --> 03:23:17,540
Oh!

3740
03:23:18,000 --> 03:23:19,020
Oh, there it is.

3741
03:23:19,500 --> 03:23:21,720
I think you did it a millisecond before I clicked.

3742
03:23:22,480 --> 03:23:23,240
Very nice.

3743
03:23:27,060 --> 03:23:28,440
Plus 12k potatoes.

3744
03:23:28,900 --> 03:23:34,260
I have no idea how much is a lot in potatoes currency.

3745
03:23:35,300 --> 03:23:35,720
Like...

3746
03:23:35,720 --> 03:23:38,240
You could say 12k or 100k and I wouldn't know.

3747
03:23:38,400 --> 03:23:38,920
Is that a lot?

3748
03:23:39,600 --> 03:23:40,680
How much do people have?

3749
03:23:45,280 --> 03:23:47,620
How many potatoes do you possess in real life right now?

3750
03:23:48,700 --> 03:23:49,120
Approximately.

3751
03:23:49,220 --> 03:23:50,000
I think I have like 8.

3752
03:23:50,520 --> 03:23:51,300
But they're big.

3753
03:23:51,440 --> 03:23:51,980
Big potatoes.

3754
03:23:52,280 --> 03:23:53,020
Baking potatoes.

3755
03:23:54,660 --> 03:23:56,360
You've never gambled and I have 40k?

3756
03:23:56,500 --> 03:23:56,700
Oh!

3757
03:23:58,240 --> 03:23:59,800
You get them just from watching, right?

3758
03:23:59,800 --> 03:24:00,200
Yeah.

3759
03:24:00,520 --> 03:24:00,620
Yeah.

3760
03:24:00,800 --> 03:24:01,000
Okay.

3761
03:24:01,240 --> 03:24:01,780
That's a lot.

3762
03:24:02,700 --> 03:24:05,580
Time to lose them all in one fell swoop.

3763
03:24:06,320 --> 03:24:07,400
By betting them all.

3764
03:24:08,720 --> 03:24:10,020
You have 5 potatoes.

3765
03:24:10,280 --> 03:24:10,420
Okay.

3766
03:24:15,370 --> 03:24:16,530
3 medium ones.

3767
03:24:17,890 --> 03:24:18,330
69.

3768
03:24:18,590 --> 03:24:19,030
Nice.

3769
03:24:21,450 --> 03:24:22,790
You have 5 pounds.

3770
03:24:22,970 --> 03:24:23,510
Wait, are you kidding?

3771
03:24:23,590 --> 03:24:25,170
Or do you actually have 5 pounds of potatoes?

3772
03:24:26,670 --> 03:24:27,990
Maybe that's not actually that much.

3773
03:24:28,030 --> 03:24:28,310
Hold on.

3774
03:24:29,950 --> 03:24:31,170
How much is that in kilos?

3775
03:24:31,170 --> 03:24:32,690
I was like a couple kilos.

3776
03:24:33,050 --> 03:24:34,050
I believe in them.

3777
03:24:34,470 --> 03:24:35,290
Sounded like way more.

3778
03:24:36,390 --> 03:24:37,570
I don't know pounds.

3779
03:24:41,110 --> 03:24:42,070
You have 6.

3780
03:24:42,390 --> 03:24:43,230
Did you count them?

3781
03:24:43,370 --> 03:24:43,750
Be honest.

3782
03:24:45,190 --> 03:24:46,290
Probably should bin them.

3783
03:24:47,070 --> 03:24:49,810
Yeah, when potatoes get old, they become nasty looking.

3784
03:24:51,410 --> 03:24:53,450
They become like aliens.

3785
03:24:54,110 --> 03:24:55,650
Weird growths out of them, you know?

3786
03:24:56,450 --> 03:24:57,330
Tentacles and shit.

3787
03:24:57,330 --> 03:24:57,870
It's weird.

3788
03:24:59,010 --> 03:25:00,110
You gotta eat them quick.

3789
03:25:01,630 --> 03:25:03,350
You can count the potatoes inside of you, yeah.

3790
03:25:09,650 --> 03:25:12,530
Dandy McGee, I would, but I don't have any bones at hand.

3791
03:25:12,670 --> 03:25:13,730
And I don't have the patience.

3792
03:25:16,930 --> 03:25:18,030
Give me soil!

3793
03:25:18,510 --> 03:25:19,130
Old potato.

3794
03:25:19,450 --> 03:25:19,850
Exactly.

3795
03:25:30,920 --> 03:25:31,720
Potato croquettes.

3796
03:25:31,920 --> 03:25:32,360
What is that?

3797
03:25:33,080 --> 03:25:34,580
I feel like I've heard that before.

3798
03:25:35,000 --> 03:25:35,400
Croquettes.

3799
03:25:37,900 --> 03:25:39,860
Ooh, those are so good!

3800
03:25:40,760 --> 03:25:42,340
I love croquettes.

3801
03:25:44,180 --> 03:25:45,760
How do you even make those?

3802
03:25:49,380 --> 03:25:51,600
Croquettes are a versatile little morsel.

3803
03:25:52,500 --> 03:25:54,740
You can fill them with ground meat, potatoes.

3804
03:25:55,080 --> 03:25:56,640
Wait, potatoes inside the potato?

3805
03:25:58,240 --> 03:25:59,360
Sign me up.

3806
03:26:00,840 --> 03:26:02,220
Croquettes are perfect.

3807
03:26:03,380 --> 03:26:04,380
That's what I have to say.

3808
03:26:05,300 --> 03:26:05,960
Exactly.

3809
03:26:05,960 --> 03:26:06,060
No.

3810
03:26:06,660 --> 03:26:07,300
Easily piss.

3811
03:26:11,030 --> 03:26:12,730
Have you eaten Hasselback potatoes?

3812
03:26:12,930 --> 03:26:13,810
Yeah, yeah, yeah, I love those.

3813
03:26:13,990 --> 03:26:17,270
Those are the ones that you cut up with a knife into small slices and put them in the oven, right?

3814
03:26:18,570 --> 03:26:19,330
Hasselhoff potatoes.

3815
03:26:22,480 --> 03:26:23,600
Those are nice.

3816
03:26:24,820 --> 03:26:25,800
Nice and crispy.

3817
03:26:28,560 --> 03:26:29,940
You made my day so much better.

3818
03:26:30,060 --> 03:26:31,180
Thank you for being a silly gamer.

3819
03:26:32,520 --> 03:26:33,800
No problem, Hive.

3820
03:26:33,960 --> 03:26:35,180
I'm glad you're enjoying it.

3821
03:26:36,000 --> 03:26:37,560
And thanks for being here, as always.

3822
03:26:38,080 --> 03:26:38,900
It's so nice.

3823
03:26:39,560 --> 03:26:41,000
Da stimme ich zu!

3824
03:26:42,980 --> 03:26:44,340
Mir stimmen alle zu.

3825
03:26:46,440 --> 03:26:48,100
Colored bundles look so cute.

3826
03:26:48,360 --> 03:26:48,980
Yeah, they do.

3827
03:26:49,180 --> 03:26:50,100
Little pouches.

3828
03:26:50,600 --> 03:26:52,080
I just love the word pouch.

3829
03:26:52,600 --> 03:26:53,520
Such a cute name.

3830
03:26:55,480 --> 03:26:58,080
Feels weird hearing you in my native language.

3831
03:26:58,520 --> 03:27:00,420
You sound just like one of my co-workers.

3832
03:27:01,540 --> 03:27:02,020
Really?

3833
03:27:04,960 --> 03:27:05,400
Nice.

3834
03:27:06,100 --> 03:27:09,500
That means I sound genuinely German then, unless you're just saying that.

3835
03:27:13,660 --> 03:27:15,200
Nice distraction from real life.

3836
03:27:15,280 --> 03:27:16,360
That's what I'm here for, man.

3837
03:27:16,860 --> 03:27:24,220
Actually, mostly I'm here for my own enjoyment, but the side effect of that seems to be having a nice effect on you, so that's good.

3838
03:27:27,520 --> 03:27:30,200
What if you just pushed the villager the whole way without using...

3839
03:27:30,200 --> 03:27:31,760
I mean, I guess I technically could.

3840
03:27:32,840 --> 03:27:34,000
But that sounds...

3841
03:27:35,480 --> 03:27:36,360
very annoying.

3842
03:27:38,600 --> 03:27:40,560
I would go nuts doing that.

3843
03:27:40,760 --> 03:27:42,160
I would actually lose my mind.

3844
03:27:45,060 --> 03:27:48,400
But the sense of accomplishment will be unbeatable if I make it.

3845
03:27:52,100 --> 03:27:54,260
Nette Coquetten hätten Dadeln im Detten.

3846
03:27:56,140 --> 03:27:57,680
Is that a tongue twister in German?

3847
03:28:02,460 --> 03:28:03,860
It was a good birthday streak.

3848
03:28:04,000 --> 03:28:04,860
Wait, it's your birthday?

3849
03:28:06,060 --> 03:28:08,120
If it is, happy birthday, Mr. Beast.

3850
03:28:10,140 --> 03:28:10,800
Or beat.

3851
03:28:12,420 --> 03:28:13,980
I'm gonna pretend you're Mr. Beast.

3852
03:28:14,220 --> 03:28:14,800
It would be funny.

3853
03:28:15,960 --> 03:28:17,160
Nah, you're not Mr. Beast.

3854
03:28:19,260 --> 03:28:20,520
Villager handling is pain.

3855
03:28:21,100 --> 03:28:22,400
They never do what you tell them.

3856
03:28:23,500 --> 03:28:24,580
Did you get your bike back already?

3857
03:28:24,760 --> 03:28:25,340
No, not yet.

3858
03:28:25,900 --> 03:28:28,320
I have to go back to my old home soon and...

3859
03:28:28,320 --> 03:28:30,000
have the moving out inspection.

3860
03:28:30,340 --> 03:28:32,940
You know, where they come and check whether or not it's all in good order.

3861
03:28:33,740 --> 03:28:35,420
And when I do that, I'm gonna bring my bike home.

3862
03:28:35,600 --> 03:28:36,260
My bike home.

3863
03:28:44,840 --> 03:28:47,240
What if we just take the village and push it somewhere else?

3864
03:28:47,540 --> 03:28:50,740
What if we just contract the space in between our villages?

3865
03:28:52,040 --> 03:28:54,140
Similar to an Alcubierre Drive.

3866
03:28:55,560 --> 03:28:57,900
I think that would... we bring the village to us, you know?

3867
03:29:00,060 --> 03:29:01,820
I will not use a boat to bring my bike.

3868
03:29:01,920 --> 03:29:03,200
I'm just gonna push the bike all the way.

3869
03:29:03,460 --> 03:29:04,580
I'm not even gonna use my hands.

3870
03:29:04,680 --> 03:29:07,120
I'm just gonna run into it with my chest and push it along.

3871
03:29:07,760 --> 03:29:11,680
And if the bike falls over onto the floor, I'm just gonna go down on the floor with it.

3872
03:29:12,460 --> 03:29:16,080
And like a floppy eel, I'm just gonna push my chest against it all the way home.

3873
03:29:22,700 --> 03:29:24,240
Full space to move the village.

3874
03:29:24,240 --> 03:29:24,760
Exactly.

3875
03:29:27,560 --> 03:29:29,100
Here's a Swedish word twister.

3876
03:29:29,480 --> 03:29:30,340
Sekslaksa in Laksaksk.

3877
03:29:30,900 --> 03:29:31,840
I can't say that.

3878
03:29:32,320 --> 03:29:35,740
I don't even know how to do a Swedish accent.

3879
03:29:37,480 --> 03:29:38,920
Bike is gonna wander away.

3880
03:29:39,040 --> 03:29:39,360
Exactly.

3881
03:29:40,420 --> 03:29:42,460
I'm imagining the bike similar to the...

3882
03:29:44,340 --> 03:29:46,240
To the urn from...

3883
03:29:47,400 --> 03:29:48,320
Ah, what's the game?

3884
03:29:48,500 --> 03:29:49,420
Deadlock, of course.

3885
03:29:49,760 --> 03:29:53,160
Every time you're not moving it, it just slowly moves back, you know?

3886
03:29:53,160 --> 03:29:54,380
If you're not close to it.

3887
03:29:55,460 --> 03:29:56,580
That's gonna be my bike.

3888
03:29:57,860 --> 03:29:59,620
Means six salmon in a salmon box.

3889
03:30:00,120 --> 03:30:00,320
Ah.

3890
03:30:01,000 --> 03:30:03,080
Well, here's a Danish one for you.

3891
03:30:04,080 --> 03:30:05,040
Uh, hold on.

3892
03:30:05,860 --> 03:30:07,040
The longest Danish word.

3893
03:30:13,560 --> 03:30:15,300
Say that three times in a row.

3894
03:30:15,520 --> 03:30:16,000
Really quickly.

3895
03:30:18,600 --> 03:30:19,620
That's a long ass word.

3896
03:30:19,620 --> 03:30:20,800
In fact, it's a...

3897
03:30:20,800 --> 03:30:23,460
It's a job position that's no longer...

3898
03:30:24,120 --> 03:30:24,700
Out there.

3899
03:30:24,820 --> 03:30:25,560
It doesn't exist anymore.

3900
03:30:27,860 --> 03:30:30,520
You get the Swedish accent if you take the potato out of your mouth.

3901
03:30:30,640 --> 03:30:31,860
I've heard so many people say that.

3902
03:30:31,960 --> 03:30:33,140
I don't think it sounds like that.

3903
03:30:33,620 --> 03:30:34,960
But I'm also a little bit biased.

3904
03:30:36,420 --> 03:30:37,360
That sounds Dutch.

3905
03:30:37,580 --> 03:30:39,160
I guess they do sound quite similar.

3906
03:30:43,750 --> 03:30:47,150
Tres tristes tigres comentrigo en un triga.

3907
03:30:50,010 --> 03:30:51,710
I butchered that so much.

3908
03:30:52,630 --> 03:30:54,050
Something something assistance.

3909
03:30:54,370 --> 03:30:55,070
You got it.

3910
03:30:58,570 --> 03:31:00,090
New mono ultra microscopic.

3911
03:31:01,470 --> 03:31:02,750
Silicovolcano coniosis.

3912
03:31:03,190 --> 03:31:04,630
That's a hard one, man.

